-- Test file for open-fact extraction in jl4-service.
--
-- This file was written for a "dynamic mode" in which UNDECLARED names with
-- inferred types were exposed as API parameters. That case no longer exists
-- here: every name below is declared (`temperature` and `humidity` once for
-- the section, `threshold` and `approved` as rule inputs), `l4 check` reports
-- nothing, and the schema of each export lists exactly the declared inputs it
-- reads. The two section-level facts were module-level ASSUMEs until
-- 2026-09-06; they are promoted to API parameters the same way.
--
-- Expected behavior:
-- - jl4-service generates a valid function schema for each export
-- - Schema includes both parameter kinds:
--   1. rule GIVEN parameters (threshold, approved)
--   2. section GIVEN parameters (humidity, temperature)

DECLARE Rating IS ONE OF Hot, Warm, Cool, Cold

§ `Climate`
    GIVEN humidity IS A NUMBER
          temperature IS A NUMBER

-- Test 1: a section-level NUMBER read next to a rule input
GIVEN threshold IS A NUMBER

@export default Check if temperature exceeds threshold
DECIDE `exceeds threshold` threshold IF temperature > threshold

-- Test 2: a rule-input BOOLEAN read beside the section-level NUMBER
@export Check if warm and approved
GIVEN approved IS A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is warm and approved` IF
      temperature > 20
  AND temperature < 30
  AND approved

-- Test 3: a rule input plus both section-level facts
-- Should have: threshold (rule GIVEN), humidity and temperature (section GIVEN)
@export Comfort check with humidity
GIVEN threshold IS A NUMBER
DECIDE `is comfortable` threshold IF
      temperature > threshold
  AND humidity < 70
